IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law (8 Del. C. ch. 1), section 204: ratification of defective corporate acts and stock.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. Source lines are lines of de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt,
-- a converter-script rendering of the Delaware Code Online (not the official text).
-- Quote lines (-- src:N | ...) are copied from that file by script.
--
-- HOW THIS MODULE IS BUILT.
--   * Every rule is a decision from facts. A judgment the text hands to the board, to the stockholders or to the Court
--     of Chancery is a plain input ("the board adopted ...", "the Court has determined otherwise").
--   * Times of day: the text speaks of "time" (validation effective time, time of the defective corporate act). This
--     module counts in days (DATE), so a comparison that turns on which of two events on the SAME day came first returns
--     NOTHING (not covered) rather than a guess. See NOTES.md, fork F-T.
--   * A rule of another section (out of this piece's range) is an input named for the fact, with a comment
--     "out of range: section N (piece X)".
--   * Section 204 applies to nonstock corporations by section 114(a) with members for stockholders, and the
--     piece-wide reading for nonstock corporations is kept in the seat layer and in section 215's module.

§ `s 204 Ratification of defective corporate acts and stock`

§§ `s 204(a) The effect of ratification or validation`

-- src:672 | (a) Subject to subsection (f) of this section, no defective corporate act or putative stock shall be void or voidable solely as a result of a failure of authorization if ratified as provided in this section or validated by the Court of Chancery in a proceeding brought under § 205 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(a) (src:672)
GIVEN `it was ratified as this section provides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was validated by the Court of Chancery in a proceeding under s 205` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(a) the defective corporate act or putative stock is shielded from being void or voidable solely for a failure of authorization` `it was ratified as this section provides` `it was validated by the Court of Chancery in a proceeding under s 205` MEANS
    `it was ratified as this section provides` OR `it was validated by the Court of Chancery in a proceeding under s 205`

§§ `s 204(b) The board's resolutions`

-- (b)(1) and (b)(2) are two routes. (b)(2) is for the election of the initial board of directors only.
-- src:673 | (b) (1) In order to ratify 1 or more defective corporate acts pursuant to this section (other than the ratification of an election of the initial board of directors pursuant to paragraph (b)(2) of this section), the board of directors of the corporation shall adopt resolutions stating:
-- src:680 | (2) In order to ratify a defective corporate act in respect of the election of the initial board of directors of the corporation pursuant to § 108 of this title, a majority of the persons who, at the time the resolutions required by this paragraph (b)(2) of this section are adopted, are exercising the powers of directors under claim and color of an election or appointment as such may adopt resolutions stating:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(b)(1) (src:673); § 204(b)(2) (src:680)
DECLARE `s 204(b) Route of ratification` IS ONE OF
    `ratifying the election of the initial board of directors under s 204(b)(2)`
    `ratifying any other defective corporate act under s 204(b)(1)`

-- src:673 | (b) (1) In order to ratify 1 or more defective corporate acts pursuant to this section (other than the ratification of an election of the initial board of directors pursuant to paragraph (b)(2) of this section), the board of directors of the corporation shall adopt resolutions stating:
-- src:674 | (A) The defective corporate act or acts to be ratified;
-- src:675 | (B) The date of each defective corporate act or acts;
-- src:676 | (C) If such defective corporate act or acts involved the issuance of shares of putative stock, the number and type of shares of putative stock issued and the date or dates upon which such putative shares were purported to have been issued;
-- src:677 | (D) The nature of the failure of authorization in respect of each defective corporate act to be ratified; and
-- src:678 | (E) That the board of directors approves the ratification of the defective corporate act or acts.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(b)(1)(A) to (E) (src:673-678)
DECLARE `s 204(b)(1) Board resolutions` HAS
    `the defective corporate act or acts to be ratified are stated`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date of each defective corporate act is stated`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the acts involved the issuance of shares of putative stock`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number and type of shares of putative stock issued and the date or dates they were purported to have been issued are stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the nature of the failure of authorization in respect of each act is stated`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the approval of the ratification by the board of directors is stated`             IS A BOOLEAN

-- (A) the acts; (B) the dates; (C) only if the acts involved the issuance of shares of putative stock, the number
-- and type of shares and the dates; (D) the nature of the failure of authorization; (E) the board approves.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(b)(1)(A) to (E) (src:673-678)
GIVEN `the resolutions` IS A `s 204(b)(1) Board resolutions`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(b)(1) the resolutions state what paragraphs (A) to (E) require` `the resolutions` MEANS
        `the resolutions`'s `the defective corporate act or acts to be ratified are stated`
    AND `the resolutions`'s `the date of each defective corporate act is stated`
    AND (   (NOT `the resolutions`'s `the acts involved the issuance of shares of putative stock`)
         OR `the resolutions`'s `the number and type of shares of putative stock issued and the date or dates they were purported to have been issued are stated`)
    AND `the resolutions`'s `the nature of the failure of authorization in respect of each act is stated`
    AND `the resolutions`'s `the approval of the ratification by the board of directors is stated`

-- The abandonment sentence. The permission comes from the resolutions themselves ("Such resolutions may also provide
-- that ..."), so without such a provision this sentence gives the board nothing. The permission runs "at any time
-- before the validation effective time". Both are days here: abandoning on the day itself cannot be told from before
-- or after, so the answer is NOTHING (fork F-T).
-- src:679 | Such resolutions may also provide that, at any time before the validation effective time in respect of any defective corporate act set forth therein, notwithstanding the approval of the ratification of such defective corporate act by stockholders, the board of directors may abandon the ratification of such defective corporate act without further action of the stockholders. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(b)(1) (src:679)
GIVEN `the resolutions provide that the board may abandon the ratification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the board abandons the ratification` IS A DATE
      `the day of the validation effective time` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(b)(1) the resolutions' abandonment provision lets the board abandon the ratification without further action of the stockholders` `the resolutions provide that the board may abandon the ratification` `the day the board abandons the ratification` `the day of the validation effective time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the resolutions provide that the board may abandon the ratification`)
            THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the day the board abandons the ratification` LESS THAN `the day of the validation effective time`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the day the board abandons the ratification` GREATER THAN `the day of the validation effective time`
            THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The board's own quorum and vote. The requirement is the one that applies to this type of act when the resolutions
-- are adopted (taken as numbers of directors, out of range: whichever provision governs the type of act), unless the
-- instruments in effect at the time of the defective act would have required a LARGER number or portion of directors
-- or of specified directors, in which case the larger applies; but the presence or approval of a director elected,
-- appointed or nominated by a class or series with no shares outstanding, or by a person who is no longer a
-- stockholder, is not required. Portions are worked out into numbers of directors by the person. The excusal reduces
-- the larger requirement by the number of such directors it counted (fork F-B).
-- src:679 | The quorum and voting requirements applicable to the ratification by the board of directors of any defective corporate act shall be the quorum and voting requirements applicable to the type of defective corporate act proposed to be ratified at the time the board adopts the resolutions ratifying the defective corporate act; provided that if the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of the corporation, any plan or agreement to which the corporation was a party or any provision of this title, in each case as in effect as of the time of the defective corporate act, would have required a larger number or portion of directors or of specified directors for a quorum to be present or to approve the defective corporate act, such larger number or portion of such directors or such specified directors shall be required for a quorum to be present or to adopt the resolutions to ratify the defective corporate act, as applicable, except that the presence or approval of any director elected, appointed or nominated by holders of any class or series of which no shares are then outstanding, or by any person that is no longer a stockholder, shall not be required.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(b)(1) (src:679)
DECLARE `s 204(b)(1) Board requirement` HAS
    `directors needed for a quorum under the requirement that applies when the resolutions are adopted` IS A NUMBER
    `directors needed to adopt the resolutions under the requirement that applies when the resolutions are adopted` IS A NUMBER
    `directors needed for a quorum under the instruments in effect at the time of the defective corporate act` IS A NUMBER
    `directors needed to adopt the resolutions under the instruments in effect at the time of the defective corporate act` IS A NUMBER
    `of those needed for a quorum, the number elected, appointed or nominated by a class or series with no shares outstanding or by a person no longer a stockholder` IS A NUMBER
    `of those needed to adopt, the number elected, appointed or nominated by a class or series with no shares outstanding or by a person no longer a stockholder` IS A NUMBER

@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(b)(1) (src:679)
GIVEN requirement IS A `s 204(b)(1) Board requirement`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 204(b)(1) the number of directors needed for a quorum to adopt the resolutions` requirement MEANS
    max (requirement's `directors needed for a quorum under the requirement that applies when the resolutions are adopted`)
        ((requirement's `directors needed for a quorum under the instruments in effect at the time of the defective corporate act`)
         MINUS (requirement's `of those needed for a quorum, the number elected, appointed or nominated by a class or series with no shares outstanding or by a person no longer a stockholder`))

@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(b)(1) (src:679)
GIVEN requirement IS A `s 204(b)(1) Board requirement`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 204(b)(1) the number of directors needed to adopt the resolutions` requirement MEANS
    max (requirement's `directors needed to adopt the resolutions under the requirement that applies when the resolutions are adopted`)
        ((requirement's `directors needed to adopt the resolutions under the instruments in effect at the time of the defective corporate act`)
         MINUS (requirement's `of those needed to adopt, the number elected, appointed or nominated by a class or series with no shares outstanding or by a person no longer a stockholder`))

@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(b)(1) (src:679)
GIVEN requirement IS A `s 204(b)(1) Board requirement`
      `the number of directors present` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors who voted to adopt the resolutions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(b)(1) the board adopted the resolutions with the quorum and vote required` requirement `the number of directors present` `the number of directors who voted to adopt the resolutions` MEANS
        `the number of directors present` AT LEAST `s 204(b)(1) the number of directors needed for a quorum to adopt the resolutions` requirement
    AND `the number of directors who voted to adopt the resolutions` AT LEAST `s 204(b)(1) the number of directors needed to adopt the resolutions` requirement

-- (b)(2): the initial board. A majority of the persons who, when the resolutions are adopted, are exercising the powers
-- of directors under claim and color of an election or appointment may adopt them. The vote is a majority of that
-- group (a base the core does not list, so the text's own words go in `named as`).
-- src:680 | (2) In order to ratify a defective corporate act in respect of the election of the initial board of directors of the corporation pursuant to § 108 of this title, a majority of the persons who, at the time the resolutions required by this paragraph (b)(2) of this section are adopted, are exercising the powers of directors under claim and color of an election or appointment as such may adopt resolutions stating:
-- src:681 | (A) The name of the person or persons who first took action in the name of the corporation as the initial board of directors of the corporation;
-- src:682 | (B) The earlier of the date on which such persons first took such action or were purported to have been elected as the initial board of directors; and
-- src:683 | (C) That the ratification of the election of such person or persons as the initial board of directors is approved.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(b)(2)(A) to (C) (src:680-683)
DECLARE `s 204(b)(2) Initial board resolutions` HAS
    `the names of the persons who first took action in the name of the corporation as the initial board of directors are stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earlier of the date those persons first took action and the date they were purported to have been elected is stated`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the approval of the ratification of their election as the initial board of directors is stated`                              IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:682 | (B) The earlier of the date on which such persons first took such action or were purported to have been elected as the initial board of directors; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(b)(2)(B) (src:682)
GIVEN `the date those persons first took action in the name of the corporation` IS A DATE
      `the date they were purported to have been elected as the initial board` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 204(b)(2)(B) the date the resolutions state` `the date those persons first took action in the name of the corporation` `the date they were purported to have been elected as the initial board` MEANS
    IF `the date those persons first took action in the name of the corporation` AT MOST `the date they were purported to have been elected as the initial board`
    THEN `the date those persons first took action in the name of the corporation`
    ELSE `the date they were purported to have been elected as the initial board`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(b)(2)(A) to (C) (src:680-683)
GIVEN resolutions IS A `s 204(b)(2) Initial board resolutions`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(b)(2) the resolutions state what paragraphs (A) to (C) require` resolutions MEANS
        resolutions's `the names of the persons who first took action in the name of the corporation as the initial board of directors are stated`
    AND resolutions's `the earlier of the date those persons first took action and the date they were purported to have been elected is stated`
    AND resolutions's `the approval of the ratification of their election as the initial board of directors is stated`

-- "A majority ... may adopt": more than half of the persons then exercising the powers of directors under claim and color.
-- The answer is NOTHING when the counts cannot be a vote (the core's `the vote carries`).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(b)(2) (src:680)
GIVEN resolutions IS A `s 204(b)(2) Initial board resolutions`
      `the number of persons exercising the powers of directors under claim and color of an election or appointment` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those persons who adopt the resolutions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(b)(2) the persons may ratify the election of the initial board by these resolutions` resolutions `the number of persons exercising the powers of directors under claim and color of an election or appointment` `the number of those persons who adopt the resolutions` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the vote carries`
                 (`a majority of` (`another base named in the provision` "the persons who, at the time the resolutions are adopted, are exercising the powers of directors under claim and color of an election or appointment as such"))
                 `the number of those persons who adopt the resolutions`
                 `the number of persons exercising the powers of directors under claim and color of an election or appointment`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST carries THEN JUST (carries AND `s 204(b)(2) the resolutions state what paragraphs (A) to (C) require` resolutions)

§§ `s 204(c) Whether the stockholders must approve`

-- Each act ratified under (b)(1) goes to the stockholders UNLESS [(1) neither this title nor the certificate, the bylaws
-- or any plan or agreement would have required stockholder approval of the act, at the time of the act or when the board
-- adopts the resolutions, (A), AND the act did not result from a failure to comply with s 203, (B)] OR [(2) when the
-- resolutions are adopted there are no shares of valid stock outstanding and entitled to vote, whether or not there are
-- shares of putative stock]. A ratification of the initial board under (b)(2) is not a "(b)(1)" ratification, so (c) does
-- not send it to the stockholders (fork F-C).
-- src:684 | (c) Each defective corporate act ratified pursuant to paragraph (b)(1) of this section shall be submitted to stockholders for approval as provided in subsection (d) of this section, unless:
-- src:685 | (1) (A) No other provision of this title, and no provision of the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of the corporation, or of any plan or agreement to which the corporation is a party, would have required stockholder approval of such defective corporate act to be ratified, either at the time of such defective corporate act or at the time the board of directors adopts the resolutions ratifying such defective corporate act pursuant to paragraph (b)(1) of this section; and
-- src:686 | (B) Such defective corporate act did not result from a failure to comply with § 203 of this title; or
-- src:687 | (2) As of the adoption of the resolutions of the board of directors adopted pursuant to paragraph (b)(1) of this section, there are no shares of valid stock outstanding and entitled to vote thereon, regardless of whether there then exist any shares of putative stock.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(c) (src:684-687)
GIVEN route IS A `s 204(b) Route of ratification`
      `no other provision of this title, the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws or a plan or agreement would have required stockholder approval of the act, at the time of the act or when the board adopts the resolutions` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: any other section of this title (pieces dg1 to dg11)
      `the act did not result from a failure to comply with s 203` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: s 203 (piece dg3)
      `when the resolutions are adopted there are no shares of valid stock outstanding and entitled to vote` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(c) the ratification must be submitted to the stockholders for approval` route `no other provision of this title, the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws or a plan or agreement would have required stockholder approval of the act, at the time of the act or when the board adopts the resolutions` `the act did not result from a failure to comply with s 203` `when the resolutions are adopted there are no shares of valid stock outstanding and entitled to vote` MEANS
    CONSIDER route
    WHEN `ratifying the election of the initial board of directors under s 204(b)(2)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `ratifying any other defective corporate act under s 204(b)(1)` THEN
        NOT (   (    `no other provision of this title, the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws or a plan or agreement would have required stockholder approval of the act, at the time of the act or when the board adopts the resolutions`
                 AND `the act did not result from a failure to comply with s 203`)
             OR `when the resolutions are adopted there are no shares of valid stock outstanding and entitled to vote`)

§§ `s 204(d) The stockholders' meeting`

-- (d)(1): due notice of the time, place (if any) and purpose of the meeting, at least 20 days before the meeting date,
-- to each holder of valid stock and putative stock, voting or nonvoting, at the address on the corporation's records.
-- (d)(3): the notice carries a copy of the resolutions (or the (b)(1)(A) to (E) information) and a statement of the
-- 120-day limit.
-- src:688 | (d) (1) If the ratification of a defective corporate act is required to be submitted to stockholders for approval pursuant to subsection (c) of this section, due notice of the time, place, if any, and purpose of the meeting shall be given at least 20 days before the date of the meeting to each holder of valid stock and putative stock, whether voting or nonvoting, at the address of such holder as it appears or most recently appeared, as appropriate, on the records of the corporation.
-- src:690 | (3) The notice shall contain a copy of the resolutions adopted by the board of directors pursuant to paragraph (b)(1) of this section or the information required by paragraphs (b)(1)(A) through (E) of this section and a statement that any claim that the defective corporate act or putative stock ratified hereunder is void or voidable due to the failure of authorization, or that the Court of Chancery should declare in its discretion that a ratification in accordance with this section not be effective or be effective only on certain conditions must be brought within 120 days from the applicable validation effective time.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(d)(1) (src:688); § 204(d)(3) (src:690)
DECLARE `s 204(d) Meeting notice` HAS
    `the day notice of the meeting was given`                                                  IS A DATE
    `the day of the meeting`                                                                   IS A DATE
    `the notice states the time of the meeting`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the meeting has a place`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice states the place of the meeting`                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice states the purpose of the meeting`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice contains a copy of the resolutions adopted under paragraph (b)(1)`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice contains the information required by paragraphs (b)(1)(A) through (E)`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice contains the statement that a claim must be brought within 120 days from the applicable validation effective time` IS A BOOLEAN

-- "At least 20 days before the date of the meeting": the notice date plus 20 days is on or before the meeting date
-- (the 20th day counts; fork F-D).
-- src:688 | due notice of the time, place, if any, and purpose of the meeting shall be given at least 20 days before the date of the meeting to each holder of valid stock and putative stock, whether voting or nonvoting, at the address of such holder as it appears or most recently appeared, as appropriate, on the records of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(d)(1) (src:688)
GIVEN notice IS A `s 204(d) Meeting notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(d)(1) due notice of the meeting was given at least 20 days before it` notice MEANS
        notice's `the day of the meeting` AT LEAST (`the date` (`period in days` 20) `after` (notice's `the day notice of the meeting was given`))
    AND notice's `the notice states the time of the meeting`
    AND (   (NOT notice's `the meeting has a place`)
         OR notice's `the notice states the place of the meeting`)
    AND notice's `the notice states the purpose of the meeting`

-- src:690 | (3) The notice shall contain a copy of the resolutions adopted by the board of directors pursuant to paragraph (b)(1) of this section or the information required by paragraphs (b)(1)(A) through (E) of this section and a statement that any claim that the defective corporate act or putative stock ratified hereunder is void or voidable due to the failure of authorization, or that the Court of Chancery should declare in its discretion that a ratification in accordance with this section not be effective or be effective only on certain conditions must be brought within 120 days from the applicable validation effective time.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(d)(3) (src:690)
GIVEN notice IS A `s 204(d) Meeting notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(d)(3) the notice contains what the paragraph requires` notice MEANS
        (   notice's `the notice contains a copy of the resolutions adopted under paragraph (b)(1)`
         OR notice's `the notice contains the information required by paragraphs (b)(1)(A) through (E)`)
    AND notice's `the notice contains the statement that a claim must be brought within 120 days from the applicable validation effective time`

-- Who is entitled to the notice. (d)(1): each holder of valid stock and of putative stock, voting or nonvoting.
-- (d)(2): ALSO the holders of record of valid stock and putative stock as of the time of the defective corporate act
-- (or the record date of the meeting, consent or other action the act involved), other than holders whose identity or
-- address cannot be determined from the corporation's records.
-- src:689 | (2) The notice shall also be given to the holders of record of valid stock and putative stock, whether voting or nonvoting, as of the time of the defective corporate act (or, in the case of any defective corporate act that involved the establishment of a record date for notice of or voting at any meeting of stockholders, for action by written consent of stockholders in lieu of a meeting, or for any other purpose, the record date for notice of or voting at such meeting, the record date for action by written consent, or the record date for such other action, as the case may be), other than holders whose identities or addresses cannot be determined from the records of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(d)(1) (src:688); § 204(d)(2) (src:689)
DECLARE `s 204(d) Holder` HAS
    `holds valid stock when notice is given, whether voting or nonvoting`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds putative stock when notice is given, whether voting or nonvoting`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `was a holder of record of valid stock or putative stock as of the time of the defective corporate act or the record date it involved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the identity and address can be determined from the records of the corporation`  IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(d)(1) (src:688); § 204(d)(2) (src:689)
GIVEN holder IS A `s 204(d) Holder`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(d)(1) and (2) the holder is entitled to notice of the meeting` holder MEANS
        holder's `holds valid stock when notice is given, whether voting or nonvoting`
    OR  holder's `holds putative stock when notice is given, whether voting or nonvoting`
    OR (    holder's `was a holder of record of valid stock or putative stock as of the time of the defective corporate act or the record date it involved`
        AND holder's `the identity and address can be determined from the records of the corporation`)

-- (d)(4): quorum and vote at the meeting. The default is the quorum and vote that apply to this type of act when the
-- ratification is approved (out of range: whichever section governs the type of act, taken as outcomes). Three
-- exceptions. a.: if the instruments in effect at the time of the defective act would have required a larger number or
-- portion of stock, of a class or series, or of specified stockholders, for a quorum or for approval, that larger
-- requirement applies, but the presence or approval of shares of a class or series with no shares outstanding, or of a
-- person no longer a stockholder, is not required (the person leaves those out of the counts behind the input).
-- b.: for the ratification of the election of a director the vote is a majority of the shares present and entitled to
-- vote on that director's election (or the larger portion the certificate or bylaws, now or at the time of the defective
-- election, required, with the same excusal). c.: if the failure of authorization was a failure to comply with s 203, the
-- vote in s 203(a)(3) is required whether or not it would have been otherwise; the text does not say it replaces the
-- other requirements, so it is taken as additional (fork F-E).
-- src:691 | (4) At such meeting, the quorum and voting requirements applicable to ratification of such defective corporate act shall be the quorum and voting requirements applicable to the type of defective corporate act proposed to be ratified at the time of the approval of the ratification, except that:
-- src:692 | a. If the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of the corporation, any plan or agreement to which the corporation was a party or any provision of this title in effect as of the time of the defective corporate act would have required a larger number or portion of stock or of any class or series thereof or of specified stockholders for a quorum to be present or to approve the defective corporate act, the presence or approval of such larger number or portion of stock or of such class or series thereof or of such specified stockholders shall be required for a quorum to be present or to approve the ratification of the defective corporate act, as applicable, except that the presence or approval of shares of any class or series of which no shares are then outstanding, or of any person that is no longer a stockholder, shall not be required;
-- src:693 | b. The approval by stockholders of the ratification of the election of a director shall require the affirmative vote of the majority of shares present at the meeting and entitled to vote on the election of such director, except that if the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of the corporation then in effect or in effect at the time of the defective election require or required a larger number or portion of stock or of any class or series thereof or of specified stockholders to elect such director, the affirmative vote of such larger number or portion of stock or of any class or series thereof or of such specified stockholders shall be required to ratify the election of such director, except that the presence or approval of shares of any class or series of which no shares are then outstanding, or of any person that is no longer a stockholder, shall not be required; and
-- src:694 | c. In the event of a failure of authorization resulting from failure to comply with the provisions of § 203 of this title, the ratification of the defective corporate act shall require the vote set forth in § 203(a)(3) of this title, regardless of whether such vote would have otherwise been required.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(d)(4) (src:691-694)
DECLARE `s 204(d)(4) Approval facts` HAS
    `the quorum required for this type of act when the ratification is approved was present`       IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: whichever section governs the type of act (pieces dg1 to dg11)
    `the vote required for this type of act when the ratification is approved was obtained`        IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: whichever section governs the type of act (pieces dg1 to dg11)
    `the defective corporate act is the election of a director`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the instruments in effect at the time of the defective corporate act required a larger quorum or vote` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that larger quorum and vote were obtained, leaving out shares of a class or series with no shares outstanding and any person no longer a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the failure of authorization resulted from a failure to comply with s 203`                     IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: s 203 (piece dg3)
    `the vote set forth in s 203(a)(3) was obtained`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: s 203(a)(3) (piece dg3)

-- b.: "the affirmative vote of the majority of shares present at the meeting and entitled to vote on the election of
-- such director". Counted in votes (s 212(a)); the core's base for "present ... and entitled to vote" is used.
-- src:693 | The approval by stockholders of the ratification of the election of a director shall require the affirmative vote of the majority of shares present at the meeting and entitled to vote on the election of such director, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(d)(4)b. (src:693)
