    IF `the shares were putative stock when the board adopted the resolutions, without giving effect to any ratification that becomes effective after that`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 204(e) The certificate of validation`

-- (e)(1): where the ratified act would have needed a s 103 certificate under another section, and either that
-- certificate needs a change to give effect to the act (including the date and time it takes effect) or none was filed
-- before, the corporation files a certificate of validation IN LIEU of the certificate the other section requires.
-- src:696 | (e) (1) If a defective corporate act ratified pursuant to this section would have required under any other section of this title the filing of a certificate in accordance with § 103 of this title, and either (i) such certificate requires any change to give effect to the defective corporate act in accordance with this section (including a change to the date and time of the effectiveness of such certificate) or (ii) a certificate was not previously filed under § 103 of this title in respect of the defective corporate act, then, in lieu of filing the certificate otherwise required by this title, the corporation shall file a certificate of validation with respect to such defective corporate act in accordance with § 103 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(e)(1) (src:696)
GIVEN `the act would have required under another section of this title the filing of a certificate in accordance with s 103` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: s 103 (piece dg1)
      `that certificate requires a change to give effect to the act in accordance with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no certificate was previously filed under s 103 in respect of the act` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: s 103 (piece dg1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(e)(1) the corporation must file a certificate of validation in lieu of the certificate the other section requires` `the act would have required under another section of this title the filing of a certificate in accordance with s 103` `that certificate requires a change to give effect to the act in accordance with this section` `no certificate was previously filed under s 103 in respect of the act` MEANS
        `the act would have required under another section of this title the filing of a certificate in accordance with s 103`
    AND (   `that certificate requires a change to give effect to the act in accordance with this section`
         OR `no certificate was previously filed under s 103 in respect of the act`)

-- (e)(2): one certificate of validation for each act, except that (i) several acts may share one if the corporation
-- filed, or to comply with this title would have filed, a single certificate under another provision to effect them, and
-- (ii) several overissues of shares of any class, classes or series may share one, the increase in authorized shares of
-- each class or series being effective as of the date of the first such overissue.
-- src:697 | (2) A separate certificate of validation shall be required for each defective corporate act requiring the filing of a certificate of validation under this section, except that (i) 2 or more defective corporate acts may be included in a single certificate of validation if the corporation filed, or to comply with this title would have filed, a single certificate under another provision of this title to effect such acts, and (ii) 2 or more overissues of shares of any class, classes or series of stock may be included in a single certificate of validation, provided that the increase in the number of authorized shares of each such class or series set forth in the certificate of validation shall be effective as of the date of the first such overissue.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(e)(2) (src:697)
GIVEN `a single certificate was filed, or would have been filed to comply with this title, under another provision to effect all the acts` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: whichever other section requires the certificate (pieces dg1 to dg11)
      `the acts are all overissues of shares of a class, classes or series of stock` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(e)(2) each of two or more acts needs its own certificate of validation` `a single certificate was filed, or would have been filed to comply with this title, under another provision to effect all the acts` `the acts are all overissues of shares of a class, classes or series of stock` MEANS
    NOT (   `a single certificate was filed, or would have been filed to comply with this title, under another provision to effect all the acts`
         OR `the acts are all overissues of shares of a class, classes or series of stock`)

-- The first overissue: the earliest of the dates (NOTHING when there are none).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(e)(2) (src:697)
GIVEN `the dates of the overissues` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 204(e)(2)(ii) the date of the first overissue` `the dates of the overissues` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the dates of the overissues`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN date FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER `s 204(e)(2)(ii) the date of the first overissue` rest
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST date
        WHEN JUST other THEN JUST (IF date AT MOST other THEN date ELSE other)

-- (e)(3): what the certificate sets forth. a. that the corporation has ratified one or more defective acts that would
-- have required a s 103 certificate; b. that each was ratified in accordance with this section; c. 1. if a certificate
-- was previously filed and needs a change: its name, title and filing date (and any certificate of correction's), a
-- statement that a certificate with all the required information is attached as an exhibit, and the date and time it is
-- deemed effective; c. 2. if no certificate was previously filed: the statement of attachment and the date and time.
-- src:698 | (3) The certificate of validation shall set forth:
-- src:699 | a. That the corporation has ratified 1 or more defective corporate acts that would have required the filing of a certificate under § 103 of this title;
-- src:700 | b. That each such defective corporate act has been ratified in accordance with this section; and
-- src:701 | c. The information required by 1 of the following paragraphs:
-- src:702 | 1. If a certificate was previously filed under § 103 of this title in respect of the defective corporate act and such certificate requires any change to give effect to the defective corporate act in accordance with this section (including a change to the date and time of the effectiveness of such certificate), the certificate of validation shall set forth:
-- src:703 | A. The name, title and filing date of the certificate so previously filed and of any certificate of correction thereto;
-- src:704 | B. A statement that a certificate containing all of the information required to be included under the applicable section or sections of this title to give effect to the defective corporate act is attached as an exhibit to the certificate of validation; and
-- src:705 | C. The date and time that such certificate shall be deemed to have become effective pursuant to this section; or
-- src:706 | 2. If a certificate was not previously filed under § 103 of this title in respect of the defective corporate act and the defective corporate act ratified pursuant to this section would have required under any other section of this title the filing of a certificate in accordance with § 103 of this title, the certificate of validation shall set forth:
-- src:707 | A. A statement that a certificate containing all of the information required to be included under the applicable section or sections of this title to give effect to the defective corporate act is attached as an exhibit to the certificate of validation, and
-- src:708 | B. The date and time that such certificate shall be deemed to have become effective pursuant to this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(e)(3) (src:698-708)
DECLARE `s 204(e)(3) Certificate of validation` HAS
    `it sets forth that the corporation has ratified 1 or more defective corporate acts that would have required the filing of a certificate under s 103` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: s 103 (piece dg1)
    `it sets forth that each such defective corporate act has been ratified in accordance with this section`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `a certificate was previously filed under s 103 in respect of the act and requires a change to give effect to it`                                       IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: s 103 (piece dg1)
    `it sets forth the name, title and filing date of the certificate previously filed and of any certificate of correction`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `it sets forth that a certificate containing all the information required is attached as an exhibit`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it sets forth the date and time the certificate shall be deemed to have become effective`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(e)(3) (src:698-708)
GIVEN certificate IS A `s 204(e)(3) Certificate of validation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(e)(3) the certificate of validation sets forth what the paragraph requires` certificate MEANS
        certificate's `it sets forth that the corporation has ratified 1 or more defective corporate acts that would have required the filing of a certificate under s 103`
    AND certificate's `it sets forth that each such defective corporate act has been ratified in accordance with this section`
    AND certificate's `it sets forth that a certificate containing all the information required is attached as an exhibit`
    AND certificate's `it sets forth the date and time the certificate shall be deemed to have become effective`
    AND (   (NOT certificate's `a certificate was previously filed under s 103 in respect of the act and requires a change to give effect to it`)
         OR certificate's `it sets forth the name, title and filing date of the certificate previously filed and of any certificate of correction`)

