§§ `s 204(g) Notice of the board's ratification`

-- The record date for this notice is the date the board adopts the resolutions, or a date within 60 days after it that
-- the board establishes ("within 60 days": the 60th day counts; fork F-D).
-- src:713 | prompt notice of the ratification shall be given to all holders of valid stock and putative stock, whether voting or nonvoting, as of the date the board of directors adopts the resolutions approving such defective corporate act, or as of a date within 60 days after such date of adoption, as established by the board of directors, at the address of such holder as it appears or most recently appeared, as appropriate, on the records of the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(g) (src:713)
GIVEN `the day the board adopts the resolutions` IS A DATE
      `the day the board establishes` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(g) the day the board establishes is the day the board adopts the resolutions or a day within 60 days after it` `the day the board adopts the resolutions` `the day the board establishes` MEANS
        `the day the board establishes` AT LEAST `the day the board adopts the resolutions`
    AND `the day the board establishes` AT MOST (`the date` (`period in days` 60) `after` `the day the board adopts the resolutions`)

-- src:713 | The notice shall also be given to the holders of record of valid stock and putative stock, whether voting or nonvoting, as of the time of the defective corporate act, other than holders whose identities or addresses cannot be determined from the records of the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(g) (src:713)
