`s 204(g) the notice is treated as notice to a holder of valid stock for the purposes of ss 222, 228, 229, 230, 232 and 233` `the recipient is a holder of putative stock, or a holder as of the time of the defective corporate act` `the purpose is subsection (d) or subsection (g) of this section` MEANS
    IF `the recipient is a holder of putative stock, or a holder as of the time of the defective corporate act`
    THEN JUST `the purpose is subsection (d) or subsection (g) of this section`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 204(a) to (f) taken together: when an act has been ratified in accordance with this section`

-- The text never lists in one place what completes a ratification. Read together, (b) (the board's resolutions), (c) and
-- (d) (the stockholders' approval, where (c) requires it), (e) (the certificate of validation, where (e)(1) requires one)
-- and (h)(6) (the validation effective time is the latest of the stockholders' approval, any time the board specified, and
-- the certificate's effectiveness) say that a ratification is accomplished when the board has adopted compliant
-- resolutions with the quorum and vote required, the stockholders have approved if (c) sends the matter to them, and the
-- certificate of validation has been filed if (e)(1) requires one, and the board has not abandoned it before the validation
-- effective time under (b)(1). Notice under (g) is a duty of its own and the text does not make a defect in it undo the
-- ratification (fork F-R). NOTHING when the stockholders' approval is not covered.
-- src:672 | Subject to subsection (f) of this section, no defective corporate act or putative stock shall be void or voidable solely as a result of a failure of authorization if ratified as provided in this section …
-- src:679 | Such resolutions may also provide that, at any time before the validation effective time in respect of any defective corporate act set forth therein, notwithstanding the approval of the ratification of such defective corporate act by stockholders, the board of directors may abandon the ratification of such defective corporate act without further action of the stockholders. …
-- src:684 | Each defective corporate act ratified pursuant to paragraph (b)(1) of this section shall be submitted to stockholders for approval as provided in subsection (d) of this section, unless:
-- src:696 | the corporation shall file a certificate of validation with respect to such defective corporate act in accordance with § 103 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(a) (src:672); § 204(b)(1) (src:679); § 204(c) (src:684); § 204(e)(1) (src:696)
GIVEN `the resolutions state what the route requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the board adopted the resolutions with the quorum and vote required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the board abandoned the ratification before the validation effective time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ratification must be submitted to the stockholders for approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholders approved the ratification` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a certificate of validation is required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of validation was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with s 103 and sets forth what s 204(e)(3) requires` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: s 103 (piece dg1)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204 the defective corporate act has been ratified in accordance with this section` `the resolutions state what the route requires` `the board adopted the resolutions with the quorum and vote required` `the board abandoned the ratification before the validation effective time` `the ratification must be submitted to the stockholders for approval` `the stockholders approved the ratification` `a certificate of validation is required` `the certificate of validation was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with s 103 and sets forth what s 204(e)(3) requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER (IF `the ratification must be submitted to the stockholders for approval`
              THEN `the stockholders approved the ratification`
              ELSE JUST TRUE)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST approved THEN
        JUST (    `the resolutions state what the route requires`
              AND `the board adopted the resolutions with the quorum and vote required`
              AND (NOT `the board abandoned the ratification before the validation effective time`)
              AND approved
              AND (   (NOT `a certificate of validation is required`)
                   OR `the certificate of validation was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with s 103 and sets forth what s 204(e)(3) requires`))

§§ `s 204(h) Definitions used in this section and in s 205 only`

-- "As used in this section and in § 205 of this title only" (src:714). Each term is worked out from facts.
-- src:714 | (h) As used in this section and in § 205 of this title only, the term:
-- src:715 | (1) “Defective corporate act” means an overissue, an election or appointment of directors that is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization, or any act or transaction purportedly taken by or on behalf of the corporation that is, and at the time such act or transaction was purportedly taken would have been, within the power of a corporation under subchapter II of this chapter (without regard to the failure of authorization identified in § 204(b)(1)(D) of this title), but is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(1) (src:714-715)
GIVEN `the act is an overissue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is an election or appointment of directors that is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or transaction was purportedly taken by or on behalf of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or transaction is, and when purportedly taken would have been, within the power of a corporation under subchapter II, without regard to the failure of authorization identified in s 204(b)(1)(D)` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: subchapter II (piece dg2)
      `the act or transaction is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(h)(1) the act is a defective corporate act` `the act is an overissue` `the act is an election or appointment of directors that is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization` `the act or transaction was purportedly taken by or on behalf of the corporation` `the act or transaction is, and when purportedly taken would have been, within the power of a corporation under subchapter II, without regard to the failure of authorization identified in s 204(b)(1)(D)` `the act or transaction is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization` MEANS
        `the act is an overissue`
    OR  `the act is an election or appointment of directors that is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization`
    OR (    `the act or transaction was purportedly taken by or on behalf of the corporation`
        AND `the act or transaction is, and when purportedly taken would have been, within the power of a corporation under subchapter II, without regard to the failure of authorization identified in s 204(b)(1)(D)`
        AND `the act or transaction is void or voidable due to a failure of authorization`)

-- (h)(2): (i) a failure to authorize or effect an act in compliance with (A) this title, (B) the certificate or bylaws,
-- or (C) a plan or agreement of the corporation or the disclosure in a proxy or consent solicitation statement, if and to
-- the extent the failure would render the act void or voidable; or (ii) a failure of the board or an officer to authorize
-- or approve an act that needed its approval for due authorization.
-- src:716 | (2) “Failure of authorization” means: (i) the failure to authorize or effect an act or transaction in compliance with (A) the provisions of this title, (B) the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of the corporation, or (C) any plan or agreement to which the corporation is a party or the disclosure set forth in any proxy or consent solicitation statement, if and to the extent such failure would render such act or transaction void or voidable; or (ii) the failure of the board of directors or any officer of the corporation to authorize or approve any act or transaction taken by or on behalf of the corporation that would have required for its due authorization the approval of the board of directors or such officer;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(2) (src:716)
GIVEN `the act failed to comply with the provisions of this title` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: the provisions of this title (pieces dg1 to dg11)
      `the act failed to comply with the certificate of incorporation or bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act failed to comply with a plan or agreement to which the corporation is a party or with the disclosure in a proxy or consent solicitation statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that failure would render the act void or voidable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the board of directors or an officer failed to authorize or approve an act that would have required for its due authorization the approval of the board of directors or of that officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(h)(2) there is a failure of authorization` `the act failed to comply with the provisions of this title` `the act failed to comply with the certificate of incorporation or bylaws` `the act failed to comply with a plan or agreement to which the corporation is a party or with the disclosure in a proxy or consent solicitation statement` `that failure would render the act void or voidable` `the board of directors or an officer failed to authorize or approve an act that would have required for its due authorization the approval of the board of directors or of that officer` MEANS
        (    (   `the act failed to comply with the provisions of this title`
              OR `the act failed to comply with the certificate of incorporation or bylaws`
              OR `the act failed to comply with a plan or agreement to which the corporation is a party or with the disclosure in a proxy or consent solicitation statement`)
         AND `that failure would render the act void or voidable`)
    OR  `the board of directors or an officer failed to authorize or approve an act that would have required for its due authorization the approval of the board of directors or of that officer`

-- (h)(3): an overissue is the purported issuance of (a) shares of a class or series in excess of the number the
-- corporation has the power to issue under s 161 at the time of the issuance, or (b) shares of a class or series not then
-- authorized for issuance by the certificate of incorporation.
-- src:717 | (3) “Overissue” means the purported issuance of:
-- src:718 | a. Shares of capital stock of a class or series in excess of the number of shares of such class or series the corporation has the power to issue under § 161 of this title at the time of such issuance; or
-- src:719 | b. Shares of any class or series of capital stock that is not then authorized for issuance by the certificate of incorporation of the corporation;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(3) (src:717-719)
GIVEN `the number of shares of the class or series purportedly issued` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares of that class or series the corporation had the power to issue under s 161 at the time of the issuance` IS A NUMBER -- out of range: s 161 (piece dg3)
      `the class or series was authorized for issuance by the certificate of incorporation at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(h)(3) the purported issuance is an overissue` `the number of shares of the class or series purportedly issued` `the number of shares of that class or series the corporation had the power to issue under s 161 at the time of the issuance` `the class or series was authorized for issuance by the certificate of incorporation at the time` MEANS
        `the number of shares of the class or series purportedly issued` GREATER THAN `the number of shares of that class or series the corporation had the power to issue under s 161 at the time of the issuance`
    OR  (NOT `the class or series was authorized for issuance by the certificate of incorporation at the time`)

-- (h)(7) valid stock: shares of any class or series of capital stock that have been duly authorized and validly issued
-- in accordance with this title.
-- src:728 | (7) “Valid stock” means the shares of any class or series of capital stock of the corporation that have been duly authorized and validly issued in accordance with this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(7) (src:728)
GIVEN `the shares are shares of a class or series of capital stock of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares have been duly authorized in accordance with this title` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: the provisions of this title (pieces dg1 to dg11)
      `the shares have been validly issued in accordance with this title` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: the provisions of this title (pieces dg1 to dg11)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(h)(7) the shares are valid stock` `the shares are shares of a class or series of capital stock of the corporation` `the shares have been duly authorized in accordance with this title` `the shares have been validly issued in accordance with this title` MEANS
        `the shares are shares of a class or series of capital stock of the corporation`
    AND `the shares have been duly authorized in accordance with this title`
    AND `the shares have been validly issued in accordance with this title`

-- (h)(4) putative stock: shares of any class or series of capital stock of the corporation (including shares issued on
-- exercise of options, rights, warrants or convertible securities, or interests in them, created or issued pursuant to a
-- defective corporate act) that (a) but for any failure of authorization would constitute valid stock, or (b) cannot be
-- determined by the board of directors to be valid stock.
-- src:720 | (4) “Putative stock” means the shares of any class or series of capital stock of the corporation (including shares issued upon exercise of options, rights, warrants or other securities convertible into shares of capital stock of the corporation, or interests with respect thereto that were created or issued pursuant to a defective corporate act) that:
-- src:721 | a. But for any failure of authorization, would constitute valid stock; or
-- src:722 | b. Cannot be determined by the board of directors to be valid stock;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(4) (src:720-722)
GIVEN `the shares are shares of a class or series of capital stock of the corporation, including shares issued on exercise of options, rights, warrants or convertible securities, or interests in them, created or issued pursuant to a defective corporate act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `but for any failure of authorization they would constitute valid stock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the board of directors cannot determine that they are valid stock` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(h)(4) the shares are putative stock` `the shares are shares of a class or series of capital stock of the corporation, including shares issued on exercise of options, rights, warrants or convertible securities, or interests in them, created or issued pursuant to a defective corporate act` `but for any failure of authorization they would constitute valid stock` `the board of directors cannot determine that they are valid stock` MEANS
        `the shares are shares of a class or series of capital stock of the corporation, including shares issued on exercise of options, rights, warrants or convertible securities, or interests in them, created or issued pursuant to a defective corporate act`
    AND (   `but for any failure of authorization they would constitute valid stock`
         OR `the board of directors cannot determine that they are valid stock`)

-- (h)(5): the date and time the act was purported to have been taken. Counted here as a day (fork F-T).
-- src:723 | (5) “Time of the defective corporate act” means the date and time the defective corporate act was purported to have been taken;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(5) (src:723)
GIVEN `the date the defective corporate act was purported to have been taken` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 204(h)(5) the time of the defective corporate act` `the date the defective corporate act was purported to have been taken` MEANS
    `the date the defective corporate act was purported to have been taken`

-- (h)(6) validation effective time: the LATEST of
--   a. when the stockholders approve (if a vote is required under (c)), or, if none is required, immediately following the
--      board's adoption of the (b)(1) or (b)(2) resolutions;
--   b. where no certificate of validation is required, the time, if any, the board specified in the resolutions, which
--      shall not precede the time of their adoption; and
--   c. the time any certificate of validation becomes effective under s 103.
-- Each is a day. A component that is still to come (the stockholders have not voted, the certificate is not yet effective)
-- makes the whole NOTHING. A time specified in the resolutions that precedes their adoption is something the text forbids
-- and gives no effect to, so the answer is NOTHING (fork F-V).
-- src:724 | (6) “Validation effective time,” with respect to any defective corporate act ratified pursuant to this section, means the latest of:
-- src:725 | a. The time at which the defective corporate act submitted to the stockholders for approval pursuant to subsection (c) of this section is approved by such stockholders or if no such vote of stockholders is required to approve the ratification of the defective corporate act, immediately following the time at which the board of directors adopts the resolutions required by paragraph (b)(1) or (b)(2) of this section;
-- src:726 | b. Where no certificate of validation is required to be filed pursuant to subsection (e) of this section, the time, if any, specified by the board of directors in the resolutions adopted pursuant to paragraph (b)(1) or (b)(2) of this section, which time shall not precede the time at which such resolutions are adopted; and
-- src:727 | c. The time at which any certificate of validation filed pursuant to subsection (e) of this section shall become effective in accordance with § 103 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(6) (src:724-727)
DECLARE `s 204(h)(6) Component` IS ONE OF
    `no time under paragraph (h)(6) applies`
    `a time under paragraph (h)(6) that is still to come`
    `a time under paragraph (h)(6)b. that precedes the adoption of the resolutions`
    `a time under paragraph (h)(6) on the day` HAS `the day` IS A DATE

@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(6) (src:724-727)
GIVEN component IS A `s 204(h)(6) Component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(h)(6) the component leaves the validation effective time undetermined` component MEANS
    CONSIDER component
    WHEN `a time under paragraph (h)(6) that is still to come` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a time under paragraph (h)(6)b. that precedes the adoption of the resolutions` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(6) (src:724-727)
GIVEN components IS A LIST OF `s 204(h)(6) Component`
GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`s 204(h)(6) the days of the components` components MEANS
    CONSIDER components
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN component FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER component
        WHEN `a time under paragraph (h)(6) on the day` day THEN day FOLLOWED BY `s 204(h)(6) the days of the components` rest
        OTHERWISE `s 204(h)(6) the days of the components` rest

@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(6) (src:724-727)
GIVEN first IS A DATE
      second IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 204(h)(6) the later of two days` first second MEANS
    IF first AT LEAST second THEN first ELSE second

@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(6) (src:724-727)
GIVEN days IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 204(h)(6) the latest of the days` days MEANS
    CONSIDER days
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN day FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER `s 204(h)(6) the latest of the days` rest
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST day
        WHEN JUST other THEN JUST (`s 204(h)(6) the later of two days` day other)

-- a.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(6)a. (src:725)
GIVEN `a stockholder vote is required under subsection (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the stockholders approved the ratification` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the board adopted the resolutions` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `s 204(h)(6) Component`
`s 204(h)(6)a. the time at which the stockholders approve or the board adopts the resolutions` `a stockholder vote is required under subsection (c)` `the day the stockholders approved the ratification` `the day the board adopted the resolutions` MEANS
    IF `a stockholder vote is required under subsection (c)`
    THEN CONSIDER `the day the stockholders approved the ratification`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `a time under paragraph (h)(6) that is still to come`
         WHEN JUST approved THEN `a time under paragraph (h)(6) on the day` approved
    ELSE `a time under paragraph (h)(6) on the day` `the day the board adopted the resolutions`

-- b. Applies only "where no certificate of validation is required", and only if the board specified a time.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(6)b. (src:726)
GIVEN `a certificate of validation is required under subsection (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the board specified in the resolutions` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the board adopted the resolutions` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `s 204(h)(6) Component`
`s 204(h)(6)b. the time the board specified in the resolutions` `a certificate of validation is required under subsection (e)` `the day the board specified in the resolutions` `the day the board adopted the resolutions` MEANS
    IF `a certificate of validation is required under subsection (e)`
    THEN `no time under paragraph (h)(6) applies`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the day the board specified in the resolutions`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `no time under paragraph (h)(6) applies`
         WHEN JUST specified THEN
             IF specified AT LEAST `the day the board adopted the resolutions`
             THEN `a time under paragraph (h)(6) on the day` specified
             ELSE `a time under paragraph (h)(6)b. that precedes the adoption of the resolutions`

-- c. Applies only if a certificate of validation is required.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(6)c. (src:727)
GIVEN `a certificate of validation is required under subsection (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the certificate of validation became effective under s 103` IS A MAYBE DATE -- out of range: s 103 (piece dg1)
GIVETH A `s 204(h)(6) Component`
`s 204(h)(6)c. the time the certificate of validation becomes effective` `a certificate of validation is required under subsection (e)` `the day the certificate of validation became effective under s 103` MEANS
    IF `a certificate of validation is required under subsection (e)`
    THEN CONSIDER `the day the certificate of validation became effective under s 103`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `a time under paragraph (h)(6) that is still to come`
         WHEN JUST effective THEN `a time under paragraph (h)(6) on the day` effective
    ELSE `no time under paragraph (h)(6) applies`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h)(6) (src:724-727)
GIVEN a IS A `s 204(h)(6) Component`
      b IS A `s 204(h)(6) Component`
      c IS A `s 204(h)(6) Component`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 204(h)(6) the day of the validation effective time` a b c MEANS
    IF `s 204(h)(6) the component leaves the validation effective time undetermined` a
       OR `s 204(h)(6) the component leaves the validation effective time undetermined` b
       OR `s 204(h)(6) the component leaves the validation effective time undetermined` c
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `s 204(h)(6) the latest of the days` (`s 204(h)(6) the days of the components` (LIST a, b, c))

-- The closing sentence of (h): "In the absence of actual fraud in the transaction, the judgment of the board of
-- directors that shares of stock are valid stock or putative stock shall be conclusive, unless otherwise determined by the
-- Court of Chancery in a proceeding brought pursuant to s 205." The Court's determination prevails; otherwise the board's
-- judgment stands unless there was actual fraud; with no judgment, or fraud and no determination, the definitions in
-- (h)(4) and (h)(7) decide and this sentence answers NOTHING.
-- src:729 | In the absence of actual fraud in the transaction, the judgment of the board of directors that shares of stock are valid stock or putative stock shall be conclusive, unless otherwise determined by the Court of Chancery in a proceeding brought pursuant to § 205 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h) (src:729)
DECLARE `s 204(h) Status of shares` IS ONE OF
    `shares that are valid stock under s 204(h)(7)`
    `shares that are putative stock under s 204(h)(4)`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(h) (src:729)
GIVEN `the judgment of the board of directors` IS A MAYBE `s 204(h) Status of shares`
      `there was actual fraud in the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court of Chancery has determined the status in a proceeding under s 205` IS A MAYBE `s 204(h) Status of shares`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 204(h) Status of shares`
`s 204(h) the status of the shares that the board's judgment makes conclusive` `the judgment of the board of directors` `there was actual fraud in the transaction` `the Court of Chancery has determined the status in a proceeding under s 205` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Court of Chancery has determined the status in a proceeding under s 205`
    WHEN JUST determined THEN JUST determined
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `there was actual fraud in the transaction`
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE `the judgment of the board of directors`

§§ `s 204(i) Ratification and validation are not the exclusive means`

-- (i): ratification under this section, or validation under s 205, is not the exclusive means of ratifying or validating
-- an act, or of adopting or endorsing an act taken in the corporation's name before it existed; and the absence or failure of
-- ratification under either does not, of itself, affect the validity of an act properly ratified under common law or
-- otherwise, nor create a presumption that an act is a defective corporate act or that stock is void or voidable.
-- src:730 | (i) Ratification under this section or validation under § 205 of this title shall not be deemed to be the exclusive means of ratifying or validating any act or transaction taken by or on behalf of the corporation, including any defective corporate act, or any issuance of stock, including any putative stock, or of adopting or endorsing any act or transaction taken by or in the name of the corporation prior to the commencement of its existence, and the absence or failure of ratification in accordance with either this section or validation under § 205 of this title shall not, of itself, affect the validity or effectiveness of any act or transaction or the issuance of any stock properly ratified under common law or otherwise, nor shall it create a presumption that any such act or transaction is or was a defective corporate act or that such stock is void or voidable.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(i) (src:730)
DECLARE `s 204(i) Means of ratifying, validating, adopting or endorsing` IS ONE OF
    `ratification under s 204`
    `validation under s 205`
    `ratification under common law or otherwise`
    `adoption or endorsement of an act taken in the name of the corporation before it began to exist`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(i) (src:730)
GIVEN means IS A `s 204(i) Means of ratifying, validating, adopting or endorsing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(i) the means is open to the corporation` means MEANS
    CONSIDER means
    WHEN `ratification under s 204` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `validation under s 205` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ratification under common law or otherwise` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `adoption or endorsement of an act taken in the name of the corporation before it began to exist` THEN TRUE

@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(i) (src:730)
GIVEN `the act or stock was properly ratified under common law or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 204(i) the absence or failure of ratification under s 204 or validation under s 205 of itself affects the validity of the act or stock` `the act or stock was properly ratified under common law or otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the act or stock was properly ratified under common law or otherwise`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref 8 Del. C. § 204(i) (src:730)
GIVEN `no ratification under s 204 or validation under s 205 has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 204(i) the absence of ratification or validation creates a presumption that the act is a defective corporate act or that the stock is void or voidable` `no ratification under s 204 or validation under s 205 has been made` MEANS
    FALSE
